today I want to talk about the  importance of storytelling so whenever  you're trying to convince anybody to do  anything whether that's a customer to  buy from you and investor to put money  into your company suppliers to give you  a good deal media to do a story on you  or you want your kids to do something  follow certain behavior you want to  persuade your husband or wife to do  something with you whenever you're  trying to persuade anybody to do  anything one of the most powerful tools  that you have in your arsenal that most  people don't use very well is  storytelling most people what they'll do  is they'll just they'll use logic  they'll use reasoning they'll give all  the reasons why you should do this but  it hits me on a very mental level  instead of an emotional level or if you  can use a story to tell me about  somebody who's gone through that and  took that action and change your life  and had success whatever the outcome is  that you're trying to accomplish if I  can connect to that person on an  emotional level if I can see myself as  that person and I want that same desired  result that I'm much more likely to take  the action that you want me to take so  here's how I stew my book in the book  there's a lot of theory there's a lot of  a lot of ideas a lot of information on  how to build and grow a business a lot  of stuff that is I don't want to see  counterintuitive but isn't necessarily  what's talked about a lot and I've use  these strategies to grow my businesses  and also help other people grow theirs  but a lot of it is theory and ideas and  just my story my sharing and what I  wanted to do was show more stories have  it be something that you guys can relate  to and so with all the points that I'm  going to be talking about what I'm going  to be doing is interviewing different  people at different stages in their  business  so this one guy who has fifteen thousand  dollars in business so he's built a full  time income for himself next one I was a  half a million dollar business than 1  million dollar business than a six  million dollar business than a 150  million dollar business and they're all  using the strategies that I talk about  in my book to build their business and  to grow and my hope is that by you not  just reading the strategies but also be  able to connect to these people  understand their stories and maybe one  or two of them you can say man that  person's just like me then you'll be  more move to take action because that's  the goal with the book I want you to  take action to grow your business to  have success to see growth to have a  meaningful impact on the world that's  the point and so whenever you try and  convince anybody to do anything you want  to use storytelling to your power the  more they can see themselves in that  story the more likely they're going to  want to take action the action that  hopefully you want them to take so as  usual it's time for Q&amp;A and I only had  one question from last week lots of  great comments but only one question as  to mark Draeger who wrote in to say am i  allergic to mosquitoes mark i am i swell  up the itch like crazy the turn all red  and then white hate them it bugs me for  days and so I try to avoid mosquitoes at  all costs and if I know I'm going to be  out with them I use sesame oil because  it acts as a natural repellent that's it  guys one question if you have a question  for me that going to answer next week  though hopefully relates to the book to  this topic or something related to  writing your own book let me know in the  comments below and next week I'll make a  video response for you thanks for  watching continue to believe and I'll  see you soon
 

